The table below shows the members of the 53rd Parliament based on the results of the 2020 general election. Ministerial roles were officially announced on 2 November 2020. Based on preliminary results, there were 40 new MPs.<ref>{{Cite news |work=[[The New Zealand Herald]] |title=Election 2020: The 40 diverse new MPs entering Parliament |url= https://www.newstalkzb.co.nz/news/vote-2020/election-2020-the-forty-newcomers-entering-parliament/ |access-date=7 November 2020|via=[[Newstalk ZB]] |date=18 October 2020}}</ref> When final results were announced on 6 November, this rose to 42 new members.<ref name=Judith>{{cite news |last1=Lynch |first1=Jenna |title=NZ Election 2020: Judith Collins will 'definitely not' stand down as leader despite National's crushing defeat |url= https://www.newshub.co.nz/home/politics/2020/11/nz-election-2020-judith-collins-will-definitely-not-stand-down-as-leader-despite-national-s-crushing-defeat.html |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20201106055203/https://www.newshub.co.nz/home/politics/2020/11/nz-election-2020-judith-collins-will-definitely-not-stand-down-as-leader-despite-national-s-crushing-defeat.html |url-status= dead |archive-date= 6 November 2020 |access-date=7 November 2020 |work=[[Newshub]] |date=6 November 2020}}</ref> Labour lost a member on 23 August 2022 due to the expulsion of Gaurav Sharma from the parliamentary party.<ref name="expulsion">{{Cite news |title=Labour's Gaurav Sharma caucus meeting live updates: Rebel MP expelled |url= https://www.newshub.co.nz/home/politics/2022/08/labour-s-gaurav-sharma-caucus-meeting-live-updates-rebel-mp-faces-expulsion.html |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20220822203948/https://www.newshub.co.nz/home/politics/2022/08/labour-s-gaurav-sharma-caucus-meeting-live-updates-rebel-mp-faces-expulsion.html |url-status= dead |archive-date= 22 August 2022 |access-date=23 August 2022 |work=[[Newshub]] |date=23 August 2022}}</ref> After Sharma's resignation from parliament, the December 2022 by-election for his [[Hamilton West (New Zealand electorate)|Hamilton West]] electorate was won by National.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2022-12-10 |title=Hamilton West by-election: National's Tama Potaka cruises to victory |url=https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/national/480491/hamilton-west-by-election-national-s-tama-potaka-cruises-to-victory |access-date=2023-01-25 |website=[[RNZ]] |language=en-nz}}</ref>

